# YouTube video titles

The title that introduces a YouTube embed must include that video's upload date in brackets at the end of the title.

Use the day, the full month name, and the year. No ordinals. The date is the video's upload date, not the post date.

```
❌ ### Extended interview: Dario Amodei (CBS Sunday Morning)
✅ ### Extended interview: Dario Amodei (CBS Sunday Morning) (13 September 2026)

❌ **How Secure is 256-bit Security?**
✅ **How Secure is 256-bit Security?** (18 March 2021)
```

A month and year already in the title is not enough. Use the full date. Do not invent a date. If the upload date cannot be checked, leave the title unchanged.
